.TH NYRQISCTL 1 "2026-08-15" "Nyrqis" "Nyrqis User Commands"
.SH NAME
nyrqisctl \- drive a running Nyrqis backend daemon's control plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nyrqisctl
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nyrqisctl
is the operator CLI for a running Nyrqis backend daemon. It drives the
daemon's main service socket (the socket
.B nyrqis_backend.py service serve
binds) over the Nyrqis IPC transport, claiming the operator identity
.RB ( host-operator ),
which the daemon authenticates by the kernel-attached uid of the caller
(the daemon's own user). It serves two services: the status service
.RB ( ping ,
.BR status ,
.BR health )
and the control plane
.RB ( containers\ list|run|kill ).
.PP
The daemon's default socket is
.B /tmp/nyrqis-status.sock
(the systemd unit serves
.BR /run/nyrqis/status.sock ).
A dedicated health-probe socket (ADR-0021), when configured, serves
.B ping/status/health
without contending with container traffic on the main socket; control
commands always use the main socket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
The daemon's main service socket (default:
.BR /tmp/nyrqis-status.sock ).
.TP
.BI \-\-health\-socket " PATH"
The daemon's dedicated health-probe socket (ADR-0021). When set,
.B ping/status/health
are routed there instead of the main
.BR \-\-socket .
Control commands refuse to use it.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
CALL timeout in seconds (default: 30).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the raw JSON reply instead of human-readable output.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Verbose (debug-level) logging.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ping
Ping the daemon; requires nothing beyond the transport's own checks.
Prints the daemon's
.B pong
reply and the resolved caller identity.
.TP
.B status
Daemon status: backend version, service version, uptime, the caller's
identity, and its capability set.
.TP
.B health
Daemon health diagnostics: serve-loop liveness, container load, IPC
registry size, state persistence, and a crash-recovery summary.
.TP
.B containers list
List the daemon's containers (id, state, pid).
.TP
.B containers run
.RI [ options ] " COMMAND " [ ARGS ...]
Spawn a container on the daemon.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Container name.
.TP
.BI \-\-capabilities " LIST"
Comma-separated data-plane capabilities (seccomp).
.TP
.B \-\-network
Give the container its own network namespace.
.TP
.BI \-\-memory " MiB"
Memory limit in MiB (default: 256).
.TP
.BI \-\-pids " N"
PID limit (default: 64).
.RE
.TP
.B containers kill " CONTAINER_ID"
Terminate a container on the daemon.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The daemon did not reply (is it running?) or the operation failed
.RB ( ok:\ false
in the reply).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown command, missing argument, or a control command
sent to
.BR \-\-health\-socket ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nyrqisctl status
nyrqisctl containers list
nyrqisctl containers run --network --memory 512 /bin/sleep 30
nyrqisctl containers kill cli-e2e
nyrqisctl --health-socket /run/nyrqis/health.sock health
nyrqisctl --json health
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nyrqis_backend (1),
.BR nyrqis-backend (8)
